-title>Phenoxodiol (2H-1-benzopyran-7-0,1,3-(4-hydroxyphenyl)), a novel isoflavone derivative, inhibits DNA topoisomerase II by stabilizing the cleavable complex</article-title><source>Anticancer Res</source><year>2002</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>2581</fpage><lpage>2585</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12529967</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gamble</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Xia</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Hahn</surname><given-names>CN</given-names></name><name><surname>Drew</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Drogemuller</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Vadas</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Phenoxodiol, an experimental anticancer drug, shows potent antiangiogenic properties in addition to its antitumour effects</article-title><source>Int J Cancer</source><year>2006</year><volume>118</volume><fpage>2412</fpage><lpage>2420</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16353157</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/ijc.21682</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kamsteeg</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Rutherford</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Sapi</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Hanczaruk</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Shahabi</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Flick</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Mor</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Phenoxodiol &#x02013; an isoflavone analog &#x02013; induces apoptosis